# Composite-key M:M join entity. Slash-form URL puts both keys as path segments:
#   /odata/CategoryCodeGroupMapping/{codeId}/{groupId}
# This shape is wired explicitly via attribute routing on the controller; the canonical OData paren
# form `/odata/CategoryCodeGroupMapping(CategoryCodeId=1,CategoryGroupId=2)` also works as alternate
# (registered via convention from the EDM HasKey declaration).
#
# No PUT or PATCH on this entity: composite-key columns are immutable (changing them is a different
# row — delete-then-create), audit columns are DB-managed, and there are no other mutable user
# fields. Also no SoftDelete column: the table has a cascading FK so its lifecycle is parent-driven,
# which means DELETE is unconditionally hard (cascade from parent removes children — no soft-delete
# trigger here, unlike Chef/CategoryCode/CategoryGroup).
@host = 127.0.01:443
@baseUrl = https://{{host}}/odata
@entitySet = CategoryCodeGroupMapping
@finalUrl = {{baseUrl}}/{{entitySet}}

###
# @name GetMetadata
GET {{baseUrl}}/$metadata HTTP/1.1
Host: {{host}}
Cache-Control: no-cache

###
# @name CreateRecord
POST {{finalUrl}} HTTP/1.1
Host: {{host}}
Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
Cache-Control: no-cache

{
	"CategoryCodeId": 1,
	"CategoryGroupId": 1
}

###
# @name ReadAllRecords
GET {{finalUrl}} HTTP/1.1
Host: {{host}}
Cache-Control: no-cache

###
# @name ReadByCompositeKey
GET {{finalUrl}}/1/1 HTTP/1.1
Host: {{host}}
Cache-Control: no-cache

###
# @name DeleteRecord
# DELETE honors If-Match — sending a stale ETag returns 412 Precondition Failed.
DELETE {{finalUrl}}/1/1 HTTP/1.1
Host: {{host}}
Cache-Control: no-cache
